From 489f81204160425b6983a4a631e1831b4bc74b78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Faris Hijazi <theefaris@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 04:58:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(fleet): show each row's machine and status, one row per
 session
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Sidebar rows for external sessions show the machine on the top line and a status
dot with Working, Needs input, Idle or Offline in place of the discovering
project's branch. Discovery now marks sessions it no longer lists offline,
replaces the legacy "[host · transport] session — title" label and the
"machine / local host" host name with the session's own values (neither was
chosen here), and hides a session that discovery reports as another connection
to a listed row (duplicateOf).

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_20cc9c1a6a80484ca54b4895500b171c
---
